---
import PortfolioPage from '../layouts/PortfolioPage.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<PortfolioPage
  title="About | Shahid Zaka"
  description="Shahid Zaka’s hands-on experience with IT support, home networking, and technical documentation."
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="portfolio-intro">
    I’m Shahid Zaka, based in Suffolk County, New York. I’m pursuing IT support
    and help desk roles, and I use this site to share my labs, projects, and
    troubleshooting write-ups.
  </p>

  <section class="portfolio-section">
    <h2>Hands-on experience</h2>
    <p>
      I’ve set up and maintained home networks, configured Wi-Fi and
      network-attached storage, and set up servers and websites for personal
      projects. I’ve also taught basic computer classes at a nonprofit in
      Brooklyn. Teaching beginners gave me practice explaining technical
      steps in plain language and adjusting my explanation when someone got stuck.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section">
    <h2>How I troubleshoot</h2>
    <p>
      I start by clarifying what someone expected to happen and what they saw
      instead. Then I check the simplest explanations first, make one change at
      a time, and verify the result. My write-ups include the checks that
      narrowed down the problem so someone else can follow the same process.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section">
    <h2>What I’m learning now</h2>
    <p>
      I’m studying for CompTIA Tech+ and building my portfolio through practical
      projects. One of those projects is this site. I set up an Astro blog on
      GitHub Pages and fixed a navigation issue that only appeared when the
      site was published under a repository path.
    </p>
    <p class="portfolio-links">
      <a href={`${base}/projects/`}>View projects</a>
      <a href={`${base}/blog/`}>Read the blog</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/szaka">Browse my GitHub</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</PortfolioPage>